TypeScript (node) example:
import { RedwoodClient, timeoutAllocator, PoolPreset } from '@redwood/inference'
const allocator = timeoutAllocator({ mode: 'interactive', baseMs: 300, jitterPercent: 8 })
const client = new RedwoodClient({ timeoutAllocator: allocator, poolPreset: PoolPreset.ProdBalanced })

// streaming reconnect with resume token handling
const stream = client.chat.stream({ model: 'gpt-open' })
stream.on('data', chunk => { /* ack and track resume cursor */ })
stream.on('error', async err => { /* backoff then resume with lastCursor */ })

Pool presets (recommended parameters):
- dev-light: {max_active: 8, max_idle: 4, conn_ttl_s: 300, idle_reap_s: 30, shards: 1}
- prod-balanced: {max_active: 64, max_idle: 16, conn_ttl_s: 900, idle_reap_s: 60, shards: 4}
- prod-high-throughput: {max_active: 256, max_idle: 64, conn_ttl_s: 1800, idle_reap_s: 120, shards: 8}
Include these presets in SDK config and Console quick-apply UI.
